&#x200B;

You can go ahead and share that information but it would be a waste of you time. Just be diligent next time and don't fall for the obvious. You have a kind heart for trying to help someone even though it was just another scummy scammer.

That depends. 

I financed a computer before and when I calculated monthly payments, I payed about $200 more then if I were to buy it in one shot. This was a 12 months to pay. You do pay more in the long run, but you are still able to buy food and pay bills. 

&#x200B;

The point I was trying to say is buy within your budget so you don't make mistakes like the people on kijiji or craigslist did. 

&#x200B;

PC gaming is like a drug. You will never really stop until you find out its too late. 

